{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1385424-backporting-some-rules-to-scion-1e","id":1385424,"title":"Backporting some rules to Scion 1e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-03T10:03:51-07:00","id":1385424,"title":"Backporting some rules to Scion 1e","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> Our Group started a new Scion Campaign from Hero on. As I'm the only one preferring 2nd edition, we stayed with 1st. But as I take the seat of the Storyteller, I've got some possibilities.<br /> <br /> 2nd editions biggest selling point for me is the setting. The World is more aware of the supernatural and the divine. So this was easy to 'backport' without needing to touch any mechanics.<br /> <br /> I always struggled with the Creature birthright and really like the attempt of 2nd edition. Creatures have no abilities, but dice pools based on their rating. On the first look, this should be doable in 1st edition with flairs as well. But I'm not sure if this will work out with game progression. So I'm interested in opinions from other people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12016-echsenkoenig","name":"Echsenkoenig","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":1,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T17:17:42-07:00","id":1385484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm the only one preferring 2nd Edition </div> </div> </div>You have my sympathies.<br /> <br /> It's a bit tough to backport rules from 2e to 1e because well, 1e's kind of built on a rocky foundation that creaks ominously.<br /> <br /> Also creatures CAN have unique abilities in 2e, reducing their dice pool and with flairs and qualities. Part of the problem is that Creatures will need an obscene amount of Epic Dex or other Epic Attributes to remain viable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:19:12-07:00","id":1385510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Echsenkoenig</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1385424-backporting-some-rules-to-scion-1e#post1385424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello everyone!<br /> <br /> Our Group started a new Scion Campaign from Hero on. As I'm the only one preferring 2nd edition, we stayed with 1st.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you tell what your group liked about 1e over 2e? It might help us better judge what needs to be preserved and how to integrate stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid"